From 783a293e7aba6e3d345f49dafcff1dca9f6277b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] feat(kernel): dump every guest thread every few seconds
 on request

A title that stops on a loading screen leaves a log that just ends, and the
watchdog samples only the thread that started it, which in a title whose
entry hands the game to a worker is parked in a host wait by then. With
RECOMP_THREAD_DUMP_SECS=n, every thread that runs guest code is listed every
n seconds: its guest registers, the kernel call it is in and the guest site
that made it, the return sites on its guest stack and, on POSIX, its host pc,
which names the lifted function a thread spins in when it makes no calls.
---
 src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c             | 262 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/thread_dump_posix/CMakeLists.txt |  14 ++
 tests/thread_dump_posix/test_main.c    | 245 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 521 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/thread_dump_posix/CMakeLists.txt
